## Unit Testing

### Writing Unit Tests

**Location**: In source files with `#[cfg(test)]` module

**Example** (`src/handlers/health.rs`):
```rust
#[cfg(test)]
mod tests {
    use super::*;
    use axum::http::StatusCode;
    
    #[tokio::test]
    async fn test_liveness_handler() {
        let response = liveness().await;
        assert_eq!(response.status(), StatusCode::OK);
        
        let body = response.into_body();
        assert!(body.is_empty());
    }
    
    #[tokio::test]
    async fn test_readiness_handler() {
        let response = readiness().await;
        assert_eq!(response.status(), StatusCode::OK);
    }
}
```

### Test Organization

```
src/
├── handlers/
│   ├── api.rs
│   │   └── mod.rs
│   │       └── #[cfg(test)] tests { ... }
│   ├── health.rs
│   │   └── #[cfg(test)] tests { ... }
{% if include_s3 %}
│   └── storage.rs
│       └── #[cfg(test)] tests { ... }
{% endif %}
```

### Running Unit Tests

```bash
# Run all unit tests
cargo test

# Run specific test
cargo test test_liveness_handler

# Run tests in module
cargo test handlers::health

# Run with output
cargo test -- --nocapture

# Run single-threaded
cargo test -- --test-threads=1
```

